1
00:00:02,290 --> 00:00:03,540
Previously on Friends:

2
00:00:03,710 --> 00:00:05,790
- I can't believe you won't be there.     - I know.

3
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:07,790
Why can't you take a couple of days off?

4
00:00:07,960 --> 00:00:10,210
- Because I can't.     - This is my wedding.

5
00:00:11,300 --> 00:00:14,050
- I can't wait to see it.     - Her parents got married there.

6
00:00:14,260 --> 00:00:17,090
It's the most beautiful place. It's right over...

7
00:00:17,470 --> 00:00:19,050
Oh, my God!

8
00:00:19,220 --> 00:00:21,970
The only thing I understand is postponing is not an option.

9
00:00:22,140 --> 00:00:23,680
This wedding is not gonna happen.

10
00:00:24,730 --> 00:00:29,690
If you don't love this, then we'll do it any other place or time. It's fine.

11
00:00:30,400 --> 00:00:31,530
It's perfect.

12
00:00:31,740 --> 00:00:33,320
- I'm going to London.     - What?

13
00:00:33,490 --> 00:00:35,780
It's not over until someone says, "I do."

14
00:00:35,950 --> 00:00:37,950
I do! I do! I do!

15
00:00:38,120 --> 00:00:39,620
Rachel, no!

16
00:00:44,870 --> 00:00:46,710
The Waltham residence.

17
00:00:46,880 --> 00:00:48,380
Hi, is this Emily's parents' house?

18
00:00:48,540 --> 00:00:50,630
This is the housekeeper.

19
00:00:50,800 --> 00:00:55,670
And, by the way, that is not how one addresses a person on the telephone.

20
00:00:56,550 --> 00:00:58,640
First one identifies oneself...

21
00:00:58,800 --> 00:01:03,020
...and then asks for the person with whom one wishes to speak.

22
00:01:03,220 --> 00:01:05,430
Um, this is Phoebe Buffay.

23
00:01:05,600 --> 00:01:07,440
I was wondering, please...

24
00:01:07,600 --> 00:01:09,690
...if it's not too much trouble, please...

25
00:01:09,860 --> 00:01:13,280
...um, might I speak with Miss Emily Waltham, please?

26
00:01:13,940 --> 00:01:16,780
Miss Waltham is at the rehearsal dinner.

27
00:01:16,950 --> 00:01:20,570
And it is not polite to make fun of people. Goodbye.

28
00:01:20,740 --> 00:01:22,910
No, no! I'll be nice, I swear.

29
00:01:23,080 --> 00:01:25,120
Could you just give me their number?

30
00:01:25,290 --> 00:01:28,830
I'm afraid I'm not at liberty to divulge that information.

31
00:01:29,000 --> 00:01:33,710
Somebody is on their way to ruin the wedding, and I have to warn them.

32
00:01:33,880 --> 00:01:36,630
So give me that number or I'll come over there...

33
00:01:36,800 --> 00:01:41,390
...and I'll kick your snooty ass all the way to New Gloukenshire!

34
00:01:42,760 --> 00:01:44,140
Hello? Hello? Oh!

35
00:01:44,310 --> 00:01:47,430
Ooh, she knew I could kick her ass.

36
00:02:38,780 --> 00:02:40,400
Hi, sweetheart.

37
00:02:40,610 --> 00:02:43,030
Mom, Dad.

38
00:02:43,200 --> 00:02:44,620
Oh, sorry, we're late.

39
00:02:44,780 --> 00:02:46,990
My fault. I insisted on riding the tube.

40
00:02:47,160 --> 00:02:49,290
Judy, the kids!

41
00:02:49,710 --> 00:02:52,540
That's what they call the subway.

42
00:02:52,710 --> 00:02:53,750
Oh!

43
00:02:53,920 --> 00:02:54,960
I thought...

44
00:02:55,130 --> 00:02:57,300
Dad, we got it.

45
00:02:57,460 --> 00:03:00,050
Oh! Here comes my dad and stepmom.

46
00:03:00,220 --> 00:03:01,430
Mr. And Mrs. Geller.

47
00:03:01,590 --> 00:03:03,510
This is Steven...

48
00:03:05,390 --> 00:03:07,350
How do you do? Very nice to meet you.

49
00:03:07,520 --> 00:03:09,390
- Ha, ha!     - Eh, darling, the Gellers.

50
00:03:09,560 --> 00:03:11,310
Darling, it's the Gellers.

51
00:03:11,480 --> 00:03:15,150
She's self-involved. I should never have married her.

52
00:03:16,320 --> 00:03:18,030
- Sorry, what?     - It's the Gellers.

53
00:03:18,190 --> 00:03:20,990
- Where?     - That's one and that's another one.

54
00:03:22,490 --> 00:03:23,780
Lovely to meet you.

55
00:03:23,950 --> 00:03:26,240
Nice of you to pay for half the wedding.

56
00:03:26,410 --> 00:03:28,950
Oh, the hell with tradition! We're happy to do it.

57
00:03:29,120 --> 00:03:31,960
Oh, we know how expensive weddings can be.

58
00:03:32,120 --> 00:03:35,170
Besides, this may be the only wedding we get to throw.

59
00:03:36,920 --> 00:03:39,090
A joke that's funny in all countries.

60
00:03:42,470 --> 00:03:44,010
Sir?

61
00:03:44,470 --> 00:03:48,010
- What's in it?     - Goat cheese, watercress and pancetta.

62
00:03:52,100 --> 00:03:53,230
That's not food.

63
00:03:53,390 --> 00:03:55,190
No, I don't want it.

64
00:03:56,980 --> 00:04:00,070
Everything's different here. I want to go home.

65
00:04:01,110 --> 00:04:03,700
I miss my family, the coffeehouse.

66
00:04:03,860 --> 00:04:06,240
I can't remember what Phoebe looks like!

67
00:04:07,620 --> 00:04:08,910
Joey, it's been three days.

68
00:04:10,660 --> 00:04:12,540
Okay, you're just a little homesick.

69
00:04:12,710 --> 00:04:16,250
Would you just try to relax and just enjoy yourself?

70
00:04:16,830 --> 00:04:18,960
You're different here too.

71
00:04:20,130 --> 00:04:22,340
You're mean in England!

72
00:04:23,630 --> 00:04:24,970
What the hell?

73
00:04:25,130 --> 00:04:26,180
What's up, Dad?

74
00:04:26,340 --> 00:04:29,140
This bill for my half. It's insane.

75
00:04:29,310 --> 00:04:31,890
Why is it so much? The reception's at their house.

76
00:04:32,060 --> 00:04:36,100
Flowers, liquor. Re-carpet first floor?

77
00:04:36,270 --> 00:04:39,020
New guest bath, landscaping.

78
00:04:39,190 --> 00:04:41,440
I'm paying to remodel this house.

79
00:04:41,610 --> 00:04:44,530
I'll give that son of a bitch a piece of my mind.

80
00:04:44,700 --> 00:04:46,240
Dad. Please.

81
00:04:46,410 --> 00:04:49,070
I don't want anything to upset Emily.

82
00:04:49,240 --> 00:04:52,290
She's had a hard enough couple of days as it is.

83
00:04:52,450 --> 00:04:54,660
Here. Let me go talk to him.

84
00:04:54,830 --> 00:04:57,120
You tell him no one takes advantage of the Gellers.

85
00:04:57,290 --> 00:04:59,840
Ooh, Jack.

86
00:05:01,210 --> 00:05:04,090
Sometimes I forget how powerful you can be.

87
00:05:08,680 --> 00:05:10,140
And I'll go get drunk.

88
00:05:16,230 --> 00:05:18,150
- Hi.     - Hello.

89
00:05:18,310 --> 00:05:19,480
Hello.

90
00:05:19,650 --> 00:05:21,690
Um, when is your next flight to London?

91
00:05:21,860 --> 00:05:24,230
- There's one leaving in 30 minutes.     - Oh!

92
00:05:24,400 --> 00:05:26,900
And I do have one seat left.

93
00:05:27,070 --> 00:05:28,610
Oh, thank you, thank you.

94
00:05:28,780 --> 00:05:32,830
The last-minute fare on this ticket is $2700.

95
00:05:33,540 --> 00:05:36,830
Ugh. I don't have enough left on my credit card.

96
00:05:37,000 --> 00:05:39,500
You can split it with another card.

97
00:05:39,670 --> 00:05:41,590
Okay, how about five?

98
00:05:43,300 --> 00:05:44,760
Oh, thank you.

99
00:05:44,920 --> 00:05:47,380
I need to see your passport.

100
00:05:50,220 --> 00:05:54,640
I don't have it, but I can tell you where it is on my nightstand.

101
00:05:56,810 --> 00:05:59,730
You know what? I have my driver's license.

102
00:05:59,900 --> 00:06:04,020
And I have a 20.

103
00:06:07,990 --> 00:06:11,570
Face it, my father is not gonna pay for the built-in barbecue.

104
00:06:11,740 --> 00:06:14,950
And believe me, you can kiss your gazebo goodbye.

105
00:06:16,500 --> 00:06:19,660
I might be able to get you the new lawn.

106
00:06:19,830 --> 00:06:22,630
Ah! Then you have to give us the lawn ornaments.

107
00:06:23,500 --> 00:06:27,420
I go back there with lawn ornaments, he'll laugh in my face.

108
00:06:28,380 --> 00:06:31,590
Will you say something, Steven?

109
00:06:32,640 --> 00:06:35,930
Don't take that tone with me.

110
00:06:36,770 --> 00:06:39,270
All right, you can.

111
00:06:42,270 --> 00:06:45,070
- Hi, Pheebs.     - Oh, thank God!

112
00:06:45,320 --> 00:06:47,570
Oh, you changed your mind. Ugh!

113
00:06:47,740 --> 00:06:50,450
You probably don't want to talk about it.

114
00:06:50,610 --> 00:06:52,610
You're doing the right thing.

115
00:06:53,370 --> 00:06:55,160
- Bye, Pheebs.     - Where are you going?

116
00:06:55,370 --> 00:06:56,790
What are you doing? No, wait.

117
00:06:57,790 --> 00:07:01,290
Why am I always pregnant when she does that?

118
00:07:03,670 --> 00:07:05,710
I'd like to toast Ross and Emily.

119
00:07:06,000 --> 00:07:07,840
My big toast is tomorrow.

120
00:07:08,010 --> 00:07:12,180
This is kind of my little toast, or Melba toast, if you will.

121
00:07:15,220 --> 00:07:16,430
Okay.

122
00:07:16,600 --> 00:07:21,560
Ahem. I knew Ross when he was, uh, going out with his first girlfriend.

123
00:07:22,940 --> 00:07:25,360
I thought things would work out until he over-inflated her.

124
00:07:30,570 --> 00:07:32,610
Oh, dear God!

125
00:07:35,740 --> 00:07:37,700
Hello, Waltham Interiors.

126
00:07:37,870 --> 00:07:39,370
Oh! Hi, Mrs. Waltham.

127
00:07:39,540 --> 00:07:43,330
I need to speak with, um, one of the best men or Ross' sister.

128
00:07:43,920 --> 00:07:48,130
- Who is this?     - Oh, Phoebe, one of Ross' best friends.

129
00:07:48,340 --> 00:07:50,590
If you're Ross' friend, why aren't you here?

130
00:07:50,760 --> 00:07:54,720
Um, I can't fly. I'm having my brother's babies.

131
00:07:59,810 --> 00:08:01,930
Am I on the radio?

132
00:08:02,640 --> 00:08:04,140
No. Um...

133
00:08:04,310 --> 00:08:06,940
...can I talk to one of them? It's important.

134
00:08:07,110 --> 00:08:10,230
I'm bored of you now. I'm going to cut you off.

135
00:08:11,900 --> 00:08:16,950
We're excited that, uh, Ross and Emily are getting married at Montgomery Hall.

136
00:08:17,120 --> 00:08:19,990
To think, my friend getting married in Monty Hall.

137
00:08:21,040 --> 00:08:22,330
Oh, come on, Monty Hall!

138
00:08:22,500 --> 00:08:25,460
Let's Make a Deal. Come on, you people!

139
00:08:26,420 --> 00:08:29,340
All right, forget it. Congratulations, Ross and Emily.

140
00:08:33,010 --> 00:08:37,090
Hey. Best man number two, Joey Tribbiani. Ha, ha.

141
00:08:37,260 --> 00:08:39,510
I'm not good with the jokes like Chandler here.

142
00:08:42,230 --> 00:08:43,680
But, uh...

143
00:08:43,850 --> 00:08:46,600
...congratulations to the happy couple.

144
00:08:47,270 --> 00:08:51,190
I first met Ross in this coffeehouse back home.

145
00:08:57,740 --> 00:08:59,490
Home.

146
00:09:00,410 --> 00:09:02,240
New York City.

147
00:09:02,410 --> 00:09:04,750
Where everybody knows my name.

148
00:09:07,540 --> 00:09:08,580
Uh, anyway...

149
00:09:08,750 --> 00:09:11,090
...uh, I love you guys.

150
00:09:11,250 --> 00:09:14,380
But not as much as I love America.

151
00:09:16,510 --> 00:09:19,220
Can we please go home now?

152
00:09:20,260 --> 00:09:22,010
Are you going home?

153
00:09:22,180 --> 00:09:24,770
I was hoping to get to know you better.

154
00:09:26,100 --> 00:09:28,650
I'm not going anywhere, sweetheart.

155
00:09:31,860 --> 00:09:33,940
I was laughing.

156
00:09:34,570 --> 00:09:36,610
Out loud?

157
00:09:37,780 --> 00:09:40,740
I didn't want everyone to think I was stupid.

158
00:09:41,280 --> 00:09:42,620
So how are you doing?

159
00:09:42,790 --> 00:09:45,410
My mom's driving me crazy. But Ross is getting married!

160
00:09:45,580 --> 00:09:47,330
I'm happy. I won't let anything spoil that.

161
00:09:49,920 --> 00:09:53,840
I just want to say that Ross is a wonderful young man.

162
00:09:54,010 --> 00:09:57,130
Oh, thanks. We like him. Ha, ha.

163
00:09:57,300 --> 00:10:01,220
My God! You must have been a teenager when you had him.

164
00:10:05,060 --> 00:10:07,770
There's no way in hell I'm paying for it.

165
00:10:07,940 --> 00:10:10,520
Look, we're down to just one point.

166
00:10:10,690 --> 00:10:13,980
Could we please just settle it after the wedding?

167
00:10:14,150 --> 00:10:17,530
Fine, but I'm not paying for your wine cellar...

168
00:10:17,700 --> 00:10:22,160
...you thieving, would-be-speaking- German-if-it-weren't-for-us man!

169
00:10:27,120 --> 00:10:31,040
The guy was hammered. There's no way you look like Ross' mother.

170
00:10:32,540 --> 00:10:35,090
- Then why would he say it?     - Because he's crazy!

171
00:10:35,250 --> 00:10:39,590
Earlier, he thanked me for my very moving performance in Titanic.

172
00:10:42,550 --> 00:10:45,430
My mother's right. I'll never get married.

173
00:10:45,600 --> 00:10:48,020
Ha! You know what, that is...

174
00:10:48,270 --> 00:10:50,350
Who wouldn't want you?

175
00:10:50,520 --> 00:10:53,860
Please! I'm a single mom with a 30-year-old son.

176
00:10:59,490 --> 00:11:00,860
I'm getting married today!

177
00:11:01,030 --> 00:11:02,110
Whoo! Heh.

178
00:11:02,780 --> 00:11:03,870
Morning.

179
00:11:04,030 --> 00:11:06,120
I'm getting married today!

180
00:11:06,290 --> 00:11:08,950
- Yeah, you are.     - Woo-hoo!

181
00:11:10,290 --> 00:11:12,420
Do you think he knew I was here?

182
00:11:20,550 --> 00:11:24,050
I've never done that with you before. Heh.

183
00:11:24,600 --> 00:11:25,930
Nope. Ha, ha.

184
00:11:26,100 --> 00:11:28,180
So, uh, how are you?

185
00:11:28,350 --> 00:11:29,970
You okay?

186
00:11:30,480 --> 00:11:31,520
Yeah, yeah.

187
00:11:31,690 --> 00:11:33,100
- You?     - Oh, yes, yes.

188
00:11:35,020 --> 00:11:36,150
You?

189
00:11:37,650 --> 00:11:39,230
We did you.

190
00:11:41,650 --> 00:11:43,360
Well...

191
00:11:44,200 --> 00:11:47,370
- I better get going.     - Oh, absolutely. Ha, ha.

192
00:11:49,750 --> 00:11:51,370
Could you not look?

193
00:11:51,750 --> 00:11:53,420
I don't want to look.

194
00:12:10,930 --> 00:12:13,440
- Uh, uh, excuse me.     - Yeah.

195
00:12:13,600 --> 00:12:15,900
If you're planning on doing that the entire flight...

196
00:12:16,060 --> 00:12:19,150
...please tell me now so that I can take a sedative.

197
00:12:19,320 --> 00:12:21,400
Or maybe slip you one.

198
00:12:23,070 --> 00:12:25,280
It's just, I'm, uh, kind of excited.

199
00:12:25,450 --> 00:12:29,780
I'm, um, going to London to, uh, tell this guy that I love him.

200
00:12:42,670 --> 00:12:45,380
- Hello.     - Where the hell have you been?

201
00:12:46,760 --> 00:12:51,350
I spent the night out. I met this cute bridesmaid. She is...

202
00:12:51,520 --> 00:12:52,810
I don't want to hear it!

203
00:12:52,980 --> 00:12:56,440
Aw, Pheebs, you know you're still my number one girl.

204
00:12:57,400 --> 00:13:01,230
We have an emergency. Rachel's coming to London.

205
00:13:01,400 --> 00:13:03,150
Oh, great!

206
00:13:03,690 --> 00:13:07,530
No, she's coming to tell Ross that she loves him.

207
00:13:07,700 --> 00:13:08,820
But he loves Emily.

208
00:13:08,990 --> 00:13:10,700
I know that!

209
00:13:11,410 --> 00:13:14,200
You have to stop her. She's going to ruin the wedding.

210
00:13:14,370 --> 00:13:16,370
Okay.

211
00:13:16,540 --> 00:13:18,500
I've done my part, okay?

212
00:13:18,670 --> 00:13:22,000
It's your responsibility now. The burden is off me.

213
00:13:22,170 --> 00:13:23,380
Right.

214
00:13:23,550 --> 00:13:25,880
So tell me about this girl.

215
00:13:29,470 --> 00:13:31,140
Hey. Have you seen Monica?

216
00:13:31,310 --> 00:13:32,890
I'm not seeing Monica.

217
00:13:36,890 --> 00:13:38,600
- What?     - What?

218
00:13:38,770 --> 00:13:39,900
Look, we gotta find her.

219
00:13:40,060 --> 00:13:42,860
Phoebe called. Rachel's coming to tell Ross she loves him.

220
00:13:43,030 --> 00:13:45,070
- Oh, my God.     - I know. We gotta find Monica.

221
00:13:45,240 --> 00:13:46,650
- Know where she is?     - No, okay?

222
00:13:46,820 --> 00:13:50,370
What's with the third degree? Why don't you just shine a light in my eyes?

223
00:13:53,160 --> 00:13:56,330
Then I realized all this stuff I had been doing...

224
00:13:56,500 --> 00:14:00,580
...proposing to Joshua, lying about why I couldn't come...

225
00:14:00,750 --> 00:14:03,550
...was all just a way of...

226
00:14:04,300 --> 00:14:06,050
I'm sorry. Can I interrupt?

227
00:14:06,220 --> 00:14:11,640
I just want to say that you are a horrible, horrible person.

228
00:14:13,140 --> 00:14:14,220
Pardon me?

229
00:14:14,390 --> 00:14:17,980
You're about to ruin the happiest day of his life.

230
00:14:18,140 --> 00:14:20,440
I have to agree with your friend Pheebs.

231
00:14:20,600 --> 00:14:24,020
This is a terrible, terrible plan.

232
00:14:24,190 --> 00:14:27,650
- But he has to know how I feel.     - But why?

233
00:14:27,820 --> 00:14:30,860
He loves this Emily. No good can come of this.

234
00:14:31,320 --> 00:14:33,830
Ugh! I think you're wrong.

235
00:14:33,990 --> 00:14:35,990
Oh, no!

236
00:14:38,790 --> 00:14:42,040
By the way, it seems to be clear you were on a break.

237
00:14:52,010 --> 00:14:54,890
Oh, my God!

238
00:14:55,060 --> 00:14:57,520
It's like a fairyland.

239
00:14:57,680 --> 00:14:59,850
I know. It's horrible, isn't it?

240
00:15:00,520 --> 00:15:03,190
I love it. I only hope my wedding looks this good.

241
00:15:03,360 --> 00:15:06,190
- Ha! I just hope...     - You can let some go by.

242
00:15:08,530 --> 00:15:09,900
Psst. Monica.

243
00:15:10,070 --> 00:15:12,030
Start looking out for Rachel.

244
00:15:12,200 --> 00:15:15,240
I'll cover the door. You watch that big hole.

245
00:15:15,410 --> 00:15:17,410
I've got Chandler covering Ross.

246
00:15:17,580 --> 00:15:20,250
Why would I care where Chandler is? Heh.

247
00:15:20,920 --> 00:15:22,830
You know, uh...

248
00:15:23,830 --> 00:15:26,090
...sometimes I don't even like Chandler.

249
00:15:27,300 --> 00:15:28,550
- Okay.     - Heh.

250
00:15:31,130 --> 00:15:32,180
I do.

251
00:15:32,930 --> 00:15:36,550
I do.

252
00:15:36,720 --> 00:15:37,930
Oh, it's the second one.

253
00:15:38,100 --> 00:15:39,390
Right?

254
00:15:43,440 --> 00:15:44,480
Hello, Joey.

255
00:15:44,650 --> 00:15:46,810
Hey, Felicity.

256
00:15:47,570 --> 00:15:50,030
Um, I thought about you all day.

257
00:15:50,190 --> 00:15:51,570
Yeah?

258
00:15:51,740 --> 00:15:53,360
Talk New York to me again.

259
00:15:54,450 --> 00:15:57,370
Forget about it.

260
00:15:57,530 --> 00:15:58,660
How you doing?

261
00:16:02,920 --> 00:16:06,080
We're not paying for your wine cellar.

262
00:16:06,250 --> 00:16:08,340
You have to meet me in the middle.

263
00:16:08,500 --> 00:16:11,380
My foot will meet the middle of your ass.

264
00:16:13,220 --> 00:16:16,470
- What's going on?     - Oh, everything's under control.

265
00:16:16,640 --> 00:16:20,140
You want a piece of me? Is that what you're saying?

266
00:16:21,060 --> 00:16:22,430
That's it!

267
00:16:22,600 --> 00:16:24,890
Parents! Parents! Back away!

268
00:16:25,060 --> 00:16:26,850
This is our wedding day!

269
00:16:27,360 --> 00:16:29,400
From now on, everyone gets along.

270
00:16:29,570 --> 00:16:31,860
And if I hear one more word...

271
00:16:32,030 --> 00:16:33,240
...no grandchildren!

272
00:16:33,400 --> 00:16:34,530
That's right!

273
00:16:34,700 --> 00:16:35,740
Okay, okay.

274
00:16:35,910 --> 00:16:37,070
Sorry, old boy.

275
00:16:37,280 --> 00:16:39,160
Sorry. Sorry.

276
00:16:40,080 --> 00:16:43,290
I could kill you with my thumb, you know.

277
00:16:46,710 --> 00:16:48,210
What was that about?

278
00:16:48,380 --> 00:16:51,340
It was this disagreement over...

279
00:16:53,220 --> 00:16:55,300
My God! You look beautiful.

280
00:16:57,680 --> 00:17:01,010
Oh! You can't see me before the wedding. It's bad luck.

281
00:17:01,180 --> 00:17:04,930
I think we've had all the bad luck we're going to have.

282
00:17:41,140 --> 00:17:43,220
My God, heh, Rachel!

283
00:17:45,730 --> 00:17:47,810
You're here. I can't believe it.

284
00:17:50,650 --> 00:17:52,270
Why are you here?

285
00:17:52,440 --> 00:17:54,610
I just came to...

286
00:17:58,530 --> 00:18:01,070
I just needed to tell you...

287
00:18:03,490 --> 00:18:06,120
...congratulations.

288
00:18:37,610 --> 00:18:39,030
Waltham Interiors.

289
00:18:39,200 --> 00:18:41,610
Mrs. Waltham? It's Phoebe.

290
00:18:41,780 --> 00:18:46,240
Can I talk to one of the best men? This is going to be the last time.

291
00:18:46,410 --> 00:18:49,500
There's a girl on the phone for you.

292
00:18:49,830 --> 00:18:51,870
Oh, great!

293
00:18:52,960 --> 00:18:54,000
Hello?

294
00:18:54,170 --> 00:18:55,500
It's Phoebe.

295
00:18:55,670 --> 00:18:57,550
Did you stop Rachel?

296
00:18:57,710 --> 00:18:59,760
But she just hugged him. That's it.

297
00:18:59,930 --> 00:19:02,180
- Nothing got ruined?     - No.

298
00:19:02,340 --> 00:19:03,930
Oh, that's so great!

299
00:19:04,100 --> 00:19:06,810
Oh! So, what's going on now?

300
00:19:08,600 --> 00:19:10,850
...I'm walking down the aisle.

301
00:19:12,770 --> 00:19:14,770
Still walking.

302
00:19:16,780 --> 00:19:18,780
Now I'm at the front with Ross.

303
00:19:18,940 --> 00:19:20,320
It's Phoebe!

304
00:19:24,910 --> 00:19:26,490
He looks pretty mad.

305
00:19:26,660 --> 00:19:28,740
Uh, I better go.

306
00:19:28,910 --> 00:19:31,410
Wait! Hold it up so I can listen.

307
00:19:38,630 --> 00:19:42,300
- What we did last night was...     - Stupid. Hmm.

308
00:19:42,470 --> 00:19:44,760
- Totally crazy, stupid.     - Ha, ha.

309
00:19:45,010 --> 00:19:47,390
What were we thinking? Heh.

310
00:19:47,890 --> 00:19:50,350
I'm coming over tonight though, right?

311
00:19:52,480 --> 00:19:53,600
Oh, yeah, definitely.

312
00:20:19,210 --> 00:20:21,260
Friends, family...

313
00:20:21,510 --> 00:20:23,550
...we are gathered to celebrate...

314
00:20:23,720 --> 00:20:26,760
...the joyous union of Ross and Emily.

315
00:20:28,350 --> 00:20:29,930
May the happiness of today...

316
00:20:30,100 --> 00:20:31,430
...be with them always.

317
00:20:31,600 --> 00:20:33,810
Now, Emily, repeat after me.

318
00:20:33,980 --> 00:20:36,480
- I, Emily.     - I, Emily.

319
00:20:36,650 --> 00:20:38,940
- Take thee, Ross.     - Take thee, Ross.

320
00:20:39,110 --> 00:20:42,110
As my lawfully wedded husband, in sickness and in health...

321
00:20:42,280 --> 00:20:44,400
...till death parts us.

322
00:20:44,570 --> 00:20:48,570
As my lawfully wedded husband, in sickness and in health...

323
00:20:48,740 --> 00:20:50,790
...until death parts us.

324
00:20:51,410 --> 00:20:52,500
Now, Ross.

325
00:20:54,210 --> 00:20:55,670
Repeat after me.

326
00:20:55,830 --> 00:20:58,830
I, Ross.

327
00:20:59,000 --> 00:21:00,500
Take thee, Emily.

328
00:21:00,670 --> 00:21:02,420
Take thee, Rachel...

329
00:21:06,390 --> 00:21:07,970
Emily!

330
00:21:13,310 --> 00:21:15,770
Ha. Emily.

331
00:21:22,610 --> 00:21:24,570
Shall I go on?

